"# UET Taxila — Scraping & Ingestion Plan\n\n**Goal:** Every useful page on `uettaxila.edu.pk` stored as clean Markdown in Convex. Re-crawling updates content, never duplicates it. PDFs are supported. Dead Letter Queue is cleared.\n\n---\n\n## Read This First\n\n- Do units in order. Each unit has one action, exact file paths, and a \"Done when\" check.\n- Do not move to the next unit if the current check fails.\n- Do not modify files not listed in a unit.\n\n---\n\n## Unit 0 — Verify the Chunk Upsert Works Correctly\n\n**Why this comes first:** Both previous plans assume the existing webhook handles upsert correctly. It does at the document level, but if old chunks are not deleted when a document is re-crawled, you get duplicate or contradictory retrieval results even though the document record looks clean. Confirm this before running any crawl.\n\n**What to do:** Open `convex/crawl/webhook.ts` and confirm where it handles an existing document. We will implement `/ingest` route and the `ingestWebhook` action which cleanly:\n1. Deletes the old `crawledChunks` rows for that document.\n2. Calls `rag.delete` to remove the old vectors from the index.\n3. Inserts the new chunks and queues them for embedding.\n\n**Done when:** You can confirm in code that re-submitting an existing URL fully replaces its chunks and vectors, not just the document record.\n\n---\n\n## Unit 1 — Update the Schema\n\n**File:** `convex/schema.ts`\n\nAdd two fields to the `documents` table and add `active` and `pending_embed` to the status field union:\n\n```typescript\ncontentHash:    v.string(),   // SHA-256 of the page markdown — skip re-embed if unchanged\ncrawlSessionId: v.string(),   // UUID of the crawl run that last saw this document\n```\n\nAdd one index:\n\n```typescript\n.index(\"by_session\", [\"crawlSessionId\"])\n```\n\n**Done when:** `npx convex dev` runs without schema errors.\n\n---\n\n## Unit 2 — Add Four Mutations\n\n**File:** `convex/crawl/mutations.ts`\n\nAdd these mutations. Do not modify existing mutations.\n\n-
